          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 61:1",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 61,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "I, Pahoran, who am the chief governor of this land, do send these words unto Moroni, the chief captain over the army. Behold, I say unto you, Moroni, that I do not joy in your great afflictions, yea, it grieves my soul.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 182,
            "end": 193,
            "text": "Alma 60:3 (3–9)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 61:2",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 61,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "But behold, there are those who do joy in your afflictions, yea, insomuch that they have risen up in rebellion against me, and also those of my people who are freemen, yea, and those who have risen up are exceedingly numerous.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 110,
            "text": "Alma 58:36; 59:13."
          },
          {
            "start": 159,
            "end": 166,
            "text": "Alma 51:6 (6–7)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 58:36; 59:13.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 58:36; 59:13",
            "references": [
              {
